Subject: [PATCH] waybar: add iOS/Darwin portability fixes

The first iOS Waybar package intentionally builds only the minimal bar surface
plus clock/custom modules. Darwin/iOS still needs a few source fixes for that
reduced set:

- use glob instead of unavailable iOS wordexp;
- provide a pipe+FD_CLOEXEC fallback for pipe2;
- avoid Linux real-time signal APIs when SIGRTMIN/SIGRTMAX are absent;
- make Darwin's WEXITSTATUS macro operate on an lvalue;
- avoid a Linux-only inotify header include;
- avoid pulling pruned Hyprland/icon-loader code through enum instantiations;
- provide the iOS timezone symbol expected by the Meson date fallback;
- tolerate missing session D-Bus/portal services for the minimal bar;
- skip the icon-loader helper whose only remaining users are pruned modules.
